Source: whatismyip
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Arghya <contact@arghyadeep.in>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/arghyadeep-k/whatismyip
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: whatismyip
Architecture: all
Depends: bash, curl, iproute2, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Print your public and local IP address(es)
 whatismyip is a small CLI tool that prints your public IPv4/IPv6
 address (via ifconfig.me, icanhazip.com, or ipinfo.io) and/or your
 local IPv4 address(es) via the system's iproute2 tools.
